From 9f1a8884357f9cc69adeb1c11a35eeeaffca67f2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 08:53:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/8] Stadium transformations: off unless a caller explicitly
 turns them on

With the setting at its default, production output changed on the 15
unfrozen-flag Pokemon Stadium games (Slippi 3.14-3.16). Fix everything
that ran with the setting off:

- admission.stadium_transformations no longer infers the setting from
  the stage and frozen flag. It returns True only for requested=True on
  an unfrozen Stadium. The base "unfrozen-stadium" admission rule is back
  for every caller that does not ask for transformations.
- validate_replay and prepare_replay_benchmark read the setting only from
  a suite entry's "stadium_transformations": true or the
  --stadium-transformations flag. Default native calls, results, stage
  names and benchmark cache keys (CACHE_VERSION 6) are the base's. Cases
  that ask run in a one-shot runner, and the benchmark skips them unless
  asked.
- The extra transforming Stadium GameData preload runs only for GameData
  loaded with MSL_GAME_DATA_STADIUM_TRANSFORMATIONS:
  - the stream runner sets it from its config's bit;
  - the server runner and msl_core_game_data_create set it only from
    MSL_STADIUM_TRANSFORMATIONS=1;
  - otherwise the preload sequence and the sealed GameData are the
    base's, and a transforming config on that GameData is refused.
- grpstadium keeps the source proc for the controller and returns early
  in 801D4548 unless the bit is set, as the base does.
- native.c reads a replay's Stadium events only when the setting is on.
- msltrace1.js takes the setting only from an explicit
  stadiumTransformations, never from isFrozenStadium.
- GrPs1-4.dat are still extracted but no longer required for a valid
  data directory.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017JX71xgnBPBiwucag1mFRr
